Sol. (b)** We know that,

\(\begin{matrix}
 & \text{~}\text{Harmonic mean}\text{~} = \frac{\sum_{}^{}\ f}{\sum_{}^{}\ \left( \frac{f}{x} \right)} \\
 & \ \therefore\ \begin{matrix}
\sum_{}^{}\ f & \  = 1 + 2 + 3 + \ldots + n = \frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\
\text{~}\text{and}\text{~}\ \sum_{}^{}\ \frac{f}{x} & \  = \frac{1}{1/2} + \frac{2}{2/3} + \frac{3}{3/4} + \ldots + \frac{n}{n/(n + 1)} \\
 & \  = 2 + \frac{3 \times 2}{2} + \frac{4 \times 3}{3} + \ldots + \frac{n(n + 1)}{n} \\
 & \  = 2 + 3 + 4 + \ldots + n + (n + 1)
\end{matrix}
\end{matrix}\)

which is an arithmetic progression with \(a = 2\) and \(d = 1\). By the formula of sum of \(n\) term of an AP,

\(\begin{matrix}
 & \ \begin{matrix}
\sum_{}^{}\ \frac{f}{x} & \  = \left\lbrack \frac{n}{2}\left\{ 2a + (n - 1)d \right\} \right\rbrack,\text{~}\text{we have}\text{~} \\
 & \  = \frac{n}{2}\left\{ 2 \times 2 + n - 1 \right\} \\
 & \  = \frac{n}{2}(3 + n) \\
\therefore & \text{~}\text{Harmonic mean}\text{~}
\end{matrix} = \frac{\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}}{\frac{n(3 + n)}{2}} \\
 & 
\end{matrix}\ \begin{matrix}
 & \  = \frac{n(n + 1) \times 2}{n(3 + n) \times 2} \\
 & \\
 & \  = \frac{n + 1}{3 + n}
\end{matrix}\)

Sol. (a)** The required mean

\(\begin{matrix}
\bar{x} & \  = \frac{1 \cdot \ ^{n}C_{1} + 2 \cdot \ ^{n}C_{2} + 3 \cdot \ ^{n}C_{3} + \ldots + n \cdot \ ^{n}C_{n}}{\ ^{n}C_{1} + \ ^{n}C_{2} + \ldots + \ ^{n}C_{n}} \\
 & \  = \frac{\sum_{r = 0}^{n} r \cdot \ ^{n}C_{r}\ \sum_{r = 1}^{n} r \cdot \frac{n}{r}\ ^{n - 1}C_{r - 1}}{\sum_{r = 1}^{n}\ ^{n}C_{r}} = \frac{n\sum_{r = 1}^{n}\ ^{n - 1}C_{r - 1}}{\sum_{r = 1}^{n}\ ^{n}C_{r}} \\
