Sol. (d)** It is given that \(\sum_{i = 1}^{n}\left( x_{i} - a \right) = n\) and \(\sum_{i = 1}^{n}\left( x_{i} - a \right)^{2} = na,(n,a > 1)\)\
\(\therefore\) Standard deviation of ' \(n\) ' observations

\(\begin{matrix}
 & \  = \sqrt{\frac{\sum_{i = 1}^{n}\left( x_{i} - a \right)^{2}}{n} - \frac{\sum_{i = 1}^{n}\left( x_{i} - a \right)}{n}} \\
 & \  = \sqrt{\frac{na}{n} - \frac{n}{n}} = \sqrt{a - 1}
\end{matrix}\)

